{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
  "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has directed the Veterans Court to take due account of the rule of prejudicial error in reviewing administrative determinations of veterans benefits. For four reasons, the court of appeals erred in holding that the Veterans Court should presume the existence of prejudice whenever it finds that the VA has erred in providing notice to the claimant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why do you say that? That it was understood so? Because of the Attorney General's commentary on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The principal reason that it was understood is because the uniform practice in the courts of appeals as of 1988 was to place upon challengers to agency action the burden of showing prejudice from the error. And the Congress was well aware of that, and in particular the Senate Veterans Affairs Committee was cited in the Ninth Circuit's decision in Seine & Line Fishermen's Union."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can we go back to the question that was just posed? We have never held that every agency -- agencies come in many sizes and shapes, but in all cases, the APA places the burden on the -- on the petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The principal reason why that error was not prejudicial is because the only way she could have received benefits for an increased rating claim was evidence that her hearing had become worse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you are talking about after the initial decision from the regional office, there is not an automatic right to a remand, but there is an automatic right to a de novo review by a more senior official at the regional office."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes. You can get a hearing. You can present new evidence. It's a decision review officer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My first question is: Is there an automatic right to a remand?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the effective date of the claim, which is the date as of which benefits are awarded, is the date the claim was filed"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government has a very strong inducement to follow the statutory obligation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the VA in all cases strives conscientiously to comply with its statutory obligations. The notice requirements as described in section 5103 are fairly vague."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher J. Meade",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "notice is integral to the system that Congress designed, the VA's failure to provide notice is likely to prejudice the veteran."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher J. Meade",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would be difficult for the veteran and comparatively easy for the government to carry a burden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is it a speculative enterprise?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher J. Meade",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Generally, though, I would agree with you that either no notice or incomplete notice are the same and would trigger a first notice error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is that such a tough thing to do? It sounds like it's sort of -- is there"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Lippmann)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two answers to that, Your Honor. The first is, the government makes the proposition that all we need to do is offer an explanation. But in legal terms, that is a proffer on appeal, and that is every bit as evidential as the actual evidence itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Then it makes sense to remand it. But if you can't do it on appeal, what sense does it make to remand it, where the same failure to provide evidence is going to doom his claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What stops you from doing that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So then why is it a big deal that you summarize what you're going to produce in the brief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You started earlier, at one point, to say how this actually worked out in your case. Could you just spend a minute to explain that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know where this first level, second level -- I'm looking at the statute on page 98a of the petition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought that was taken out, the fourth one. No?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When you have been saying \"entitled to a lawyer,\" do you mean entitled to a lawyer or allowed to have a lawyer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Miller)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6117a950b5de-0002-0009",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Given the volume of cases that the VA confronts, there is a serious harm to the system in unnecessary remands that have to be given priority over other cases and that divert resources from the adjudication of meritorious claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1209",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "6117a950b5dedb37839ba287a7d83fff7fe802d7b48dd61bfe044427aa8730b9",
